  "body": "Maintainer request from #1452 (\"We should be able to load DXF file to do profile cuts on.\").\n\nDepends on #1862.\n\n## Goal\nExpose `.dxf` import in `camcraft-ui` (`Model > Open` and viewport drop), ask the user for units when `$INSUNITS` is absent, show sketches in the browser tree, and draw sketch chains on the setup XY plane.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `.dxf` to `pick_mesh_file` (or generalize to `pick_model_file`) in `crates/ui/src/state.rs` so `Model > Open` accepts DXF files.\n- Route `.dxf` files dropped on the viewport (`#1450`) through the same DXF import command flow.\n- Keep `ImportFixture` on `.dxf` refused by name until `#744` adds fixture profile support.\n- Detect the typed missing-units error from #1862 inside `finish_import`, display drawing bounding dimensions in both millimeters and inches, ask the user to choose `Millimeters` or `Inches`, and then execute `ImportDxf` onto undo history. Never guess units silently.\n- Show the import summary (units, layer count, chain counts, open chains, and skipped annotation counts) in the status message.\n- Show imported sketches in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/browser_tree.rs` with hide/show visibility toggles, selection, delete, and move/setup alignment actions.\n- Render sketch curves (`Line`, `Arc`, `Circle`, `Polyline`) on the setup XY plane via `collect_overlay` in `crates/ui/src/interact.rs` transformed by `Location` and setup alignment. Mark open chain endpoints with a clear distinct symbol so open gaps never look closed.\n\n## Done means\nUsers open or drag-and-drop a `.dxf` file, answer the `Millimeters`/`Inches` modal on unitless files, toggle sketch visibility in the browser tree, see sketch curves aligned on XY with distinct open-chain endpoint markers, and remove the sketch with Ctrl+Z; headless UI tests pin import, missing-units dialog, browser row, and viewport overlay segments.\n\nPart of #1452\n",
